From: Edward <edward@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: hdmi: attach Broadcast RGB property and default to Full range

Rockchip VOP2 outputs full-range (0-255) RGB pixels without hardware
full-to-limited RGB compression, while drm_hdmi_state_helper defaults
Broadcast RGB to Automatic (setting is_limited_range=y and AVI Q1Q0=01
for CEA modes), which causes displays with selectable quantization
range (QS=1) to crush 0-16 blacks.

Attach the "Broadcast RGB" connector property in drmm_connector_hdmi_init()
and default hdmi.broadcast_rgb to DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_FULL in
__drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_reset(). This also satisfies
hdmi_dolby_vision_check()'s full-range RGB requirement without breaking
YUV limited-range output.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_connector.c
@@ -649,6 +649,10 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	ret = drm_connector_attach_broadcast_rgb_property(connector);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	connector->hdmi.funcs = hdmi_funcs;
 
 	return 0;
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
@@ -323,6 +323,6 @@
 	new_conn_state->max_bpc = max_bpc;
 	new_conn_state->max_requested_bpc = max_bpc;
-	new_conn_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb = DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_AUTO;
+	new_conn_state->hdmi.broadcast_rgb = DRM_HDMI_BROADCAST_RGB_FULL;
 	new_conn_state->hdmi.dolby_vision = DRM_HDMI_DOLBY_VISION_OFF;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(__drm_atomic_helper_connector_hdmi_reset);
